# CODEOWNERS — coverage model (un-inverted).
#
# DEFAULT = UNOWNED: any path not matched below needs no code-owner review, so a
# low-risk deterministic PR (and a Margot LOW-risk verdict) can merge without the
# operator. There is deliberately NO `* @owner` catch-all — this repository's
# ordinary content and docs flow unattended.
#
# OWNED (listed below) = the safety / identity / gate machinery: a judgment change
# there must have a human. The branch ruleset requires code-owner review (with 0
# baseline approvals), so touching an owned path holds the PR for @{{OWNER}};
# touching only unowned paths does not.
#
# When adding a path: uncertain -> OWNED (under-coverage — an owned path left
# unowned — is the dangerous direction). Anchored patterns (/path/ or /file) over
# bare names. Every path added here must also be declared in
# lexijamesesq/dotty's rulesets/default-branch.json under this repo's
# `codeowners_owned`, or the estate's drift check reports the two as diverged.

# --- Gate machinery (CI/gate/hook chain and its configs) ---
/.github/workflows/            @{{OWNER}}
/.pre-commit-config.yaml       @{{OWNER}}

# --- Gate/lint configs that can DISABLE a check (gate self-protection) ---
/.gitleaks.toml                @{{OWNER}}
/.gitleaks.ci.toml             @{{OWNER}}
/.house-code.json              @{{OWNER}}

# --- Governance, policy & identity ---
/.github/CODEOWNERS            @{{OWNER}}

# UNOWNED by default (flow without the operator): README.md, LICENSE, CLAUDE.md,
# and every ordinary content, code, docs and cosmetic file. When this repo
# gains a tracked Claude Code settings file under /.claude/, own it here (and
# in the declaration): the seed does not list it, because the estate's
# sample-shape hook refuses a CODEOWNERS reference to a config the repo does
# not track.
